        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "rendered. Good luck, the result of ( lit stored by ) past",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "religious performances fructifies for man seasonably, as do",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "trees.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "102. Meritorious deeds done in a former life protect a man in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "a forest, on a battlefield, in the midst of foes, or water or fire,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "in the vast ocean, or on a mountain-top, whether he be asleep",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "or careless or in a perilous condition.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "103. O good man, to obtain your cherished desire, adore",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "that goddess—Good conduct—that changes wicked men into",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "good, fools into wise men, enemies into friends, the invisible",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "into the visible and deadly poison into nectar, in an instant.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Fix not your hopes on numerous other qualities with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "persistent application.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "104. When good luck is favourable to one ( lit. closely",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "linked ), a splendid mansion, sportive women, and prosperity",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "brilliant with the white umbrella—all these things are en-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "joyed for a long time; but when unfavourable ( lit. when its",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "thread is snapped ) behold ! all these vanish in all directions",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "like a wreath of pearls, the thread of which is broken in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "sport of amorous quarrels.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "105. A wise man, bent on doing a thing, good or bad,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "should first carefully consider its consequence. The issue of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "actions done in hot haste becomes, till death, like a dart,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "poignant to the heart.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "106. The luckless man that does not practise penance",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "on coming into this Land of karman, cooks ( as it were )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "with sandal-wood &c. for fuel, in a utensil made of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Vaidûrya gem, the oil-cake of sesamum; or ploughs the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "earth with a golden ploughshare for the sake of the root of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "the arka tree, or makes a hedge round a crop of kodravas of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "camphor-trees having cut them down.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
